INT. FUNERAL HOME EMBALMING ROOM - NIGHT

White tile. Steel table. A single fluorescent tube hums over a sheeted body. The wall clock reads 3:12.

HOLLIS PRUITT, 50s, the funeral director, stands at the table in a rubber apron. He is calm. He has done this thousands of times.

MARGUERITE DUBOIS, 30s, his apprentice, holds a clipboard. She watches the sheet.

KENJI SAITO, 40s, the night janitor, mops the corner. He keeps his eyes on the floor.

ABIGAIL TRENT, 60s, the widow, sits on a folding chair by the door. A black purse in her lap.

OLUWASEUN "SEUN" ADEBAYO, 20s, her grandson, leans on the wall beside her. Arms crossed.

REVEREND CALDER MOSS, 70s, stands in the doorway, Bible pressed to his chest.

MARGUERITE
Mrs. Trent, you really shouldn't be in here.

ABIGAIL
I want to see him.

HOLLIS
He isn't ready, ma'am.

ABIGAIL
I said I want to see him.

Hollis glances at the Reverend. The Reverend nods. Hollis lifts the sheet to the chin.

The face is grey. Peaceful. She leans in and touches his cheek.

The finger comes away wet.

ABIGAIL (CONT'D)
He's warm.

HOLLIS
That's the lights, Mrs. Trent.

SEUN
Grandma, come on.

She doesn't move. Kenji's mop stops.

The body's chest rises.

Marguerite drops the clipboard. It CLATTERS across the tile.

MARGUERITE
Did you see that?

HOLLIS
Nobody breathe.

They don't. The fluorescent tube FLICKERS.

The chest rises again. Slowly. The sheet slides off the shoulder.

The Reverend begins to pray, fast, under his breath. Seun backs into the wall. Kenji drops the mop and edges toward the door.

Hollis presses two fingers to the neck. His face goes blank. He pulls back.

HOLLIS (CONT'D)
No pulse.

MARGUERITE
Then what's moving?

The mouth opens. A long, wet exhale. Then a whisper, dry as paper, with no voice behind it.

She stands. The purse falls. She is smiling.

ABIGAIL
Walter.

SEUN
Grandma, don't.

The lights die. Total dark. Footsteps. A scrape of metal.

Light snaps back. The table is empty. The sheet lies folded at the foot.

Kenji laughs, high and cracked. Hollis grabs him by the shoulder. He stops.

The Reverend lowers his Bible. Marguerite is staring at the wet footprints that lead across the tile to the open back door.

Abigail is gone. Seun runs after her into the night.
